<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Posts on Anurag Pratik</title><link>https://anuragprat1k.github.io/posts/</link><description>Recent content in Posts on Anurag Pratik</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 09 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://anuragprat1k.github.io/posts/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Reckoning with Multiple Myeloma</title><link>https://anuragprat1k.github.io/posts/multiple-myeloma/</link><pubDate>Thu, 09 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://anuragprat1k.github.io/posts/multiple-myeloma/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This is a notebook of me trying to understand the important aspects of multiple myeloma - the basics of cell biology, what turns a healthy cell cancerous, how myeloma is diagnosed, how it is treated, how we know those treatments work through clinical trials, where care is heading, and how treatment differs in the US and India.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="basics-of-cell-biology"&gt;Basics of cell biology&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cancer originates from a malfunction in the cell biology. So it is important to understand the basic machinery of the cell first, which I reduce here crudely into its form and function.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>LLM Architectures, FLOP-Matched</title><link>https://anuragprat1k.github.io/posts/llm-architectures/</link><pubDate>Thu, 09 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://anuragprat1k.github.io/posts/llm-architectures/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;The dense backbone from Llama-2 is the de facto standard for modern LLMs, and Mixtral-style sparse MoE is the dominant paradigm at open-weight frontier scale. I wanted to implement both, and their predecessor, GPT-2 and see how the architectural differences between each contribute to a toy task — pretraining on TinyStories at FLOP-matched compute.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 680 560" role="img" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="arch-svg" style="width:100%;height:auto;max-width:760px;display:block;margin:1.5em auto;font-family:-apple-system,'system-ui','Segoe UI',sans-serif"&gt;
 &lt;title&gt;Architectural progression: GPT-2 to Llama-2 to Mixtral full models&lt;/title&gt;
 &lt;desc&gt;Three models side by side. Each shows a transformer block (norm, attention, norm, MLP/MoE) repeated N times, followed by a final norm and a linear LM head. GPT-2 uses LayerNorm, multi-head attention, LayerNorm, and a GELU MLP. Llama-2 replaces all four with RMSNorm, grouped-query attention with RoPE, RMSNorm, and a SwiGLU MLP. Mixtral keeps Llama-2's norm and attention but swaps the MLP for a sparse mixture-of-experts layer.&lt;/desc&gt;
